{
  "version": 8,
  "name": "Peregrine OSM overlay (OpenMapTiles)",
  "metadata": {
    "peregrine:note": "peregrine-osm.json rewritten for use as an OVERLAY over another map. Two differences, and nothing else: there is no `background` layer, because an overlay clearing the canvas would erase the map under it; and the opaque ground fills (landcover, landuse, park) are gone, water is a wash rather than a colour, and a building is its outline. What is left is the linework and the names, which is what a chart adds to a shaded relief or an image."
  },
  "sources": {
    "openmaptiles": {
      "type": "vector"
    }
  },
